| Layer | Choice |
|---|---|
| App | Next.js 16 App Router, React 19, TypeScript |
| Styling | Tailwind + a small `components/ui` kit (button, card, input, etc.) |
| Auth + data | Supabase (Auth, Postgres, RLS, storage) |
| Payments | Stripe |
| AI | OpenRouter (`lib/ai/client.ts`), model from `AI_MODEL` (defaults to `openrouter/free`) |
| File parsing | `pdfjs-dist` for PDFs, `jszip` for `.pptx` XML |
| Package manager | pnpm |

## User flow

1. **Landing** (`/`) → register / login
2. **Upload** a PDF or PPTX (`/upload`)
3. Server extracts text, then AI **map-reduces** it into topics
4. Student picks topics and format (`/documents/[id]/quiz/new`)
5. AI generates questions; student takes the quiz (`/quizzes/[id]`)
6. Free-response answers are AI-graded; results + history live at `/quizzes/[id]/results` and `/history`
7. **Billing** is Basic vs Pro via Stripe (`/billing`)

The signed-in chrome is `AppShell` + sidebar. Session refresh is in `proxy.ts` (Next 16’s proxy, not the older `middleware.ts`).

## Domain model

The core tables in `types/database.ts` / `supabase/migrations`:

- **users** — email, Stripe customer, `subscription_status` (`basic` | `pro`)
- **documents** — file, type (`pdf` | `pptx`), status (`processing` | `ready` | `error`), optional `processing_warnings`
- **topics** — title, summary `content`, verbatim `source_content` (used for quiz generation)
- **quizzes** — format, status, score
- **quiz_questions** / **quiz_answers**
- **usage_records** — monthly quiz / document / question counts

RLS is per-user throughout. Migrations go `00001` → `00006`; later ones add quiz error status, rename free→basic, topic source text, and processing warnings.

